{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reactor hosts live world and video models. You describe a scene. Then you open a session and stream video. You can steer the stream with a new prompt."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactorWorld()"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateWorld()"},{"type":"text","value":" for navigable worlds. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactorVideo()"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateLiveVideo()"},{"type":"text","value":" for live video models. Both mint a session token. Neither supports "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-reactor\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-reactor\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-reactor\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-reactor\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-reactor\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-reactor\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-reactor\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-reactor\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Peer dependency: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai"},{"type":"text","value":". The browser also needs "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@reactor-team/js-sdk"},{"type":"text","value":" to connect and play the stream. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../media/world-generation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"World Generation"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"link","href":"../media/live-generation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Live Generation"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A full working app is in "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/ts-react-media","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/ts-react-media"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Open the World or Live tab."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"api-key","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API key"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create a key in the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://www.reactor.inc/dashboard","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reactor dashboard"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Keys start with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rk_"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The example app uses "},{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/byok","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bring Your Own Key"}]},{"type":"text","value":". The browser pastes the key. The relay reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x-byok-reactor"},{"type":"text","value":", then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"REACTOR_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateWorld } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from '@tanstack/ai/byok/server'\nimport { reactorWorld } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor'\nimport { reactorByok } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor/byok'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, reactorByok)\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(reactorByok)\n\n  const world = await generateWorld({\n    adapter: reactorWorld('visko-orbis-stable', { apiKey }),\n    prompt: 'A neon cyberpunk city at night, slow aerial drift',\n  })\n\n  return Response.json({\n    token: world.token,\n    model: world.model,\n    prompt: world.prompt,\n    expiresAt: world.expiresAt,\n  })\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter mints a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"session-scoped"}]},{"type":"text","value":" token for that model only. Hand "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"world.token"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"world.model"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"world.prompt"},{"type":"text","value":" to the browser. Do not put the API key in the JSON body."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"models","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Models"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass a string literal so TypeScript can narrow options."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { reactorWorld } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor'\n\nconst adapter = reactorWorld('visko-orbis-stable')","lang":"ts"},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Connect slug"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"visko-orbis-stable"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactor/visko-orbis-stable"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"visko-orbis-dynamic"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactor/visko-orbis-dynamic"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"happy-oyster-adventure"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactor/happy-oyster-adventure"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"happy-oyster-director"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactor/happy-oyster-director"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lingbot-world-2"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactor/lingbot-world-2"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lingbot"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactor/lingbot"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"helios"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactor/helios"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"world.model"},{"type":"text","value":" is the connect slug. Pass it to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"new Reactor({ modelName })"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"live-video","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Live video"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reactor video is a live stream, not a finished file. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateLiveVideo()"},{"type":"text","value":" returns a token. The browser connects, sets the prompt, and plays the track."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateLiveVideo } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { reactorVideo } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor'\n\nconst apiKey = process.env.REACTOR_API_KEY ?? ''\nconst live = await generateLiveVideo({\n  adapter: reactorVideo('helios', { apiKey }),\n  prompt: 'A neon cyberpunk city at night, slow aerial drift',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hand "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"live.token"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"live.model"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"live.prompt"},{"type":"text","value":" to the browser. Connect as shown in "},{"type":"link","href":"../media/live-generation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Live Generation"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Connect slug"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"helios"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactor/helios"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fast-h3"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactor/fast-h3"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"longlive-v2"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactor/longlive-v2"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ltx2"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactor/ltx2"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"helios"},{"type":"text","value":" also works with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactorWorld()"},{"type":"text","value":". Pick "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateLiveVideo()"},{"type":"text","value":" when you want a video session. Pick "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateWorld()"},{"type":"text","value":" when you want a navigable world."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass a text prompt to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateWorld()"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateLiveVideo()"},{"type":"text","value":". Those calls mint a token. They do not send resolution or a seed image."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"connect"},{"type":"text","value":", send browser commands. LingBot starts from a seed image. Pass a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"File"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<input type=\"file\">"},{"type":"text","value":". The SDK uploads it and returns a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FileRef"},{"type":"text","value":". Do not send base64. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start"},{"type":"text","value":" also needs "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"set_prompt"},{"type":"text","value":". Write the prompt to describe what the image shows."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Reactor } from '@reactor-team/js-sdk'\n\nconst reactor = new Reactor({ modelName: 'reactor/lingbot' })\nconst picker = document.querySelector('input[type=\"file\"]')\nif (!(picker instanceof HTMLInputElement)) {\n  throw new Error('Pick a seed image')\n}\nconst file = picker.files?.[0]\nif (file === undefined) {\n  throw new Error('Pick a seed image')\n}\nconst image = await reactor.uploadFile(file)\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_image', { image })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_prompt', {\n  prompt: 'A narrow stone alley at night, wet cobbles, one lit shop window.',\n})\nawait reactor.sendCommand('start', {})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Helios can take the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"File"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"set_conditioning"},{"type":"text","value":" so prompt and image land together."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Orbis takes an optional seed image. Send "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"set_image"},{"type":"text","value":" before "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"set_prompt"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start"},{"type":"text","value":". Use a 16:9 image, because Orbis resizes other shapes without a crop. A new image during a run has no effect until "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reset"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"browser-session-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Browser session options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Orbis reads these on the next "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start"},{"type":"text","value":". Keep them in client state. Send them with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sendCommand"},{"type":"text","value":" after "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"connect"},{"type":"text","value":". They are not token-mint fields."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Reactor } from '@reactor-team/js-sdk'\n\nconst reactor = new Reactor({ modelName: 'reactor/visko-orbis-stable' })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_resolution', { resolution: '2k' })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_seed', { seed: 42 })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_audio_enabled', { audio_enabled: true })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Command"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resolution"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"set_resolution"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1080p"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"2k"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"4k"},{"type":"text","value":" delivery tier"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"seed"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"set_seed"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"RNG seed for the next run"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"audioEnabled"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"set_audio_enabled"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":", skip audio compute"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"audioPrompt"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"set_audio_prompt"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sound description, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"\""},{"type":"text","value":" for picture-driven audio"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"custom-endpoint","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom endpoint"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { reactorWorld } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor'\n\nconst apiKey = process.env.REACTOR_API_KEY ?? ''\nconst adapter = reactorWorld('visko-orbis-stable', {\n  apiKey,\n  baseUrl: 'https://api.reactor.inc',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-you-have-now","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What you have now"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A server call that mints a scoped Reactor token for one world or video model. Next: connect in the browser as shown in "},{"type":"link","href":"../media/world-generation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"World Generation"}]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"link","href":"../media/live-generation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Live Generation"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"api-key","text":"API key","level":2},{"id":"models","text":"Models","level":2},{"id":"live-video","text":"Live video","level":2},{"id":"browser-session-options","text":"Browser session options","level":2},{"id":"custom-endpoint","text":"Custom endpoint","level":2},{"id":"what-you-have-now","text":"What you have now","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nReactor hosts live world and video models. You describe a scene. Then you open a session and stream video. You can steer the stream with a new prompt.\n\nUse `reactorWorld()` with `generateWorld()` for navigable worlds. Use `reactorVideo()` with `generateLiveVideo()` for live video models. Both mint a session token. Neither supports `chat()`.\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-reactor\nvue: @tanstack/ai-reactor\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-reactor\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-reactor\npreact: @tanstack/ai-reactor\nangular: @tanstack/ai-reactor\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-reactor\noctane: @tanstack/ai-reactor\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nPeer dependency: `@tanstack/ai`. The browser also needs `@reactor-team/js-sdk` to connect and play the stream. See [World Generation](../media/world-generation) and [Live Generation](../media/live-generation).\n\nA full working app is in [`examples/ts-react-media`](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/ts-react-media). Open the World or Live tab.\n\n## API key\n\nCreate a key in the [Reactor dashboard](https://www.reactor.inc/dashboard). Keys start with `rk_`.\n\nThe example app uses [Bring Your Own Key](../advanced/byok). The browser pastes the key. The relay reads `x-byok-reactor`, then `REACTOR_API_KEY`.\n\n```ts\nimport { generateWorld } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from '@tanstack/ai/byok/server'\nimport { reactorWorld } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor'\nimport { reactorByok } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor/byok'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, reactorByok)\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(reactorByok)\n\n  const world = await generateWorld({\n    adapter: reactorWorld('visko-orbis-stable', { apiKey }),\n    prompt: 'A neon cyberpunk city at night, slow aerial drift',\n  })\n\n  return Response.json({\n    token: world.token,\n    model: world.model,\n    prompt: world.prompt,\n    expiresAt: world.expiresAt,\n  })\n}\n```\n\nThe adapter mints a **session-scoped** token for that model only. Hand `world.token`, `world.model`, and `world.prompt` to the browser. Do not put the API key in the JSON body.\n\n## Models\n\nPass a string literal so TypeScript can narrow options.\n\n```ts\nimport { reactorWorld } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor'\n\nconst adapter = reactorWorld('visko-orbis-stable')\n```\n\n| Id | Connect slug |\n| --- | --- |\n| `visko-orbis-stable` | `reactor/visko-orbis-stable` |\n| `visko-orbis-dynamic` | `reactor/visko-orbis-dynamic` |\n| `happy-oyster-adventure` | `reactor/happy-oyster-adventure` |\n| `happy-oyster-director` | `reactor/happy-oyster-director` |\n| `lingbot-world-2` | `reactor/lingbot-world-2` |\n| `lingbot` | `reactor/lingbot` |\n| `helios` | `reactor/helios` |\n\n`world.model` is the connect slug. Pass it to `new Reactor({ modelName })`.\n\n## Live video\n\nReactor video is a live stream, not a finished file. `generateLiveVideo()` returns a token. The browser connects, sets the prompt, and plays the track.\n\n```ts\nimport { generateLiveVideo } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { reactorVideo } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor'\n\nconst apiKey = process.env.REACTOR_API_KEY ?? ''\nconst live = await generateLiveVideo({\n  adapter: reactorVideo('helios', { apiKey }),\n  prompt: 'A neon cyberpunk city at night, slow aerial drift',\n})\n```\n\nHand `live.token`, `live.model`, and `live.prompt` to the browser. Connect as shown in [Live Generation](../media/live-generation).\n\n| Id | Connect slug |\n| --- | --- |\n| `helios` | `reactor/helios` |\n| `fast-h3` | `reactor/fast-h3` |\n| `longlive-v2` | `reactor/longlive-v2` |\n| `ltx2` | `reactor/ltx2` |\n\n`helios` also works with `reactorWorld()`. Pick `generateLiveVideo()` when you want a video session. Pick `generateWorld()` when you want a navigable world.\n\nPass a text prompt to `generateWorld()` / `generateLiveVideo()`. Those calls mint a token. They do not send resolution or a seed image.\n\nAfter `connect`, send browser commands. LingBot starts from a seed image. Pass a `File` from `<input type=\"file\">`. The SDK uploads it and returns a `FileRef`. Do not send base64. `start` also needs `set_prompt`. Write the prompt to describe what the image shows.\n\n```ts\nimport { Reactor } from '@reactor-team/js-sdk'\n\nconst reactor = new Reactor({ modelName: 'reactor/lingbot' })\nconst picker = document.querySelector('input[type=\"file\"]')\nif (!(picker instanceof HTMLInputElement)) {\n  throw new Error('Pick a seed image')\n}\nconst file = picker.files?.[0]\nif (file === undefined) {\n  throw new Error('Pick a seed image')\n}\nconst image = await reactor.uploadFile(file)\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_image', { image })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_prompt', {\n  prompt: 'A narrow stone alley at night, wet cobbles, one lit shop window.',\n})\nawait reactor.sendCommand('start', {})\n```\n\nHelios can take the same `File` with `set_conditioning` so prompt and image land together.\n\nOrbis takes an optional seed image. Send `set_image` before `set_prompt` and `start`. Use a 16:9 image, because Orbis resizes other shapes without a crop. A new image during a run has no effect until `reset`.\n\n## Browser session options\n\nOrbis reads these on the next `start`. Keep them in client state. Send them with `sendCommand` after `connect`. They are not token-mint fields.\n\n```ts\nimport { Reactor } from '@reactor-team/js-sdk'\n\nconst reactor = new Reactor({ modelName: 'reactor/visko-orbis-stable' })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_resolution', { resolution: '2k' })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_seed', { seed: 42 })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_audio_enabled', { audio_enabled: true })\n```\n\n| Option | Command | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `resolution` | `set_resolution` | `1080p`, `2k`, or `4k` delivery tier |\n| `seed` | `set_seed` | RNG seed for the next run |\n| `audioEnabled` | `set_audio_enabled` | When `false`, skip audio compute |\n| `audioPrompt` | `set_audio_prompt` | Sound description, or `\"\"` for picture-driven audio |\n\n## Custom endpoint\n\n```ts\nimport { reactorWorld } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor'\n\nconst apiKey = process.env.REACTOR_API_KEY ?? ''\nconst adapter = reactorWorld('visko-orbis-stable', {\n  apiKey,\n  baseUrl: 'https://api.reactor.inc',\n})\n```\n\n## What you have now\n\nA server call that mints a scoped Reactor token for one world or video model. Next: connect in the browser as shown in [World Generation](../media/world-generation) or [Live Generation](../media/live-generation).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Reactor\nid: reactor-adapter\ndescription: \"Generate live worlds and video with Reactor models in TanStack AI via the @tanstack/ai-reactor adapter.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - reactor\n  - world generation\n  - live generation\n  - orbis\n  - helios\n  - generateWorld\n  - generateLiveVideo\n  - adapter\n---\n\nReactor hosts live world and video models. You describe a scene. Then you open a session and stream video. You can steer the stream with a new prompt.\n\nUse `reactorWorld()` with `generateWorld()` for navigable worlds. Use `reactorVideo()` with `generateLiveVideo()` for live video models. Both mint a session token. Neither supports `chat()`.\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-reactor\nvue: @tanstack/ai-reactor\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-reactor\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-reactor\npreact: @tanstack/ai-reactor\nangular: @tanstack/ai-reactor\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-reactor\noctane: @tanstack/ai-reactor\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nPeer dependency: `@tanstack/ai`. The browser also needs `@reactor-team/js-sdk` to connect and play the stream. See [World Generation](../media/world-generation) and [Live Generation](../media/live-generation).\n\nA full working app is in [`examples/ts-react-media`](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/ts-react-media). Open the World or Live tab.\n\n## API key\n\nCreate a key in the [Reactor dashboard](https://www.reactor.inc/dashboard). Keys start with `rk_`.\n\nThe example app uses [Bring Your Own Key](../advanced/byok). The browser pastes the key. The relay reads `x-byok-reactor`, then `REACTOR_API_KEY`.\n\n```ts\nimport { generateWorld } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from '@tanstack/ai/byok/server'\nimport { reactorWorld } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor'\nimport { reactorByok } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor/byok'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, reactorByok)\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(reactorByok)\n\n  const world = await generateWorld({\n    adapter: reactorWorld('visko-orbis-stable', { apiKey }),\n    prompt: 'A neon cyberpunk city at night, slow aerial drift',\n  })\n\n  return Response.json({\n    token: world.token,\n    model: world.model,\n    prompt: world.prompt,\n    expiresAt: world.expiresAt,\n  })\n}\n```\n\nThe adapter mints a **session-scoped** token for that model only. Hand `world.token`, `world.model`, and `world.prompt` to the browser. Do not put the API key in the JSON body.\n\n## Models\n\nPass a string literal so TypeScript can narrow options.\n\n```ts\nimport { reactorWorld } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor'\n\nconst adapter = reactorWorld('visko-orbis-stable')\n```\n\n| Id | Connect slug |\n| --- | --- |\n| `visko-orbis-stable` | `reactor/visko-orbis-stable` |\n| `visko-orbis-dynamic` | `reactor/visko-orbis-dynamic` |\n| `happy-oyster-adventure` | `reactor/happy-oyster-adventure` |\n| `happy-oyster-director` | `reactor/happy-oyster-director` |\n| `lingbot-world-2` | `reactor/lingbot-world-2` |\n| `lingbot` | `reactor/lingbot` |\n| `helios` | `reactor/helios` |\n\n`world.model` is the connect slug. Pass it to `new Reactor({ modelName })`.\n\n## Live video\n\nReactor video is a live stream, not a finished file. `generateLiveVideo()` returns a token. The browser connects, sets the prompt, and plays the track.\n\n```ts\nimport { generateLiveVideo } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { reactorVideo } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor'\n\nconst apiKey = process.env.REACTOR_API_KEY ?? ''\nconst live = await generateLiveVideo({\n  adapter: reactorVideo('helios', { apiKey }),\n  prompt: 'A neon cyberpunk city at night, slow aerial drift',\n})\n```\n\nHand `live.token`, `live.model`, and `live.prompt` to the browser. Connect as shown in [Live Generation](../media/live-generation).\n\n| Id | Connect slug |\n| --- | --- |\n| `helios` | `reactor/helios` |\n| `fast-h3` | `reactor/fast-h3` |\n| `longlive-v2` | `reactor/longlive-v2` |\n| `ltx2` | `reactor/ltx2` |\n\n`helios` also works with `reactorWorld()`. Pick `generateLiveVideo()` when you want a video session. Pick `generateWorld()` when you want a navigable world.\n\nPass a text prompt to `generateWorld()` / `generateLiveVideo()`. Those calls mint a token. They do not send resolution or a seed image.\n\nAfter `connect`, send browser commands. LingBot starts from a seed image. Pass a `File` from `<input type=\"file\">`. The SDK uploads it and returns a `FileRef`. Do not send base64. `start` also needs `set_prompt`. Write the prompt to describe what the image shows.\n\n```ts\nimport { Reactor } from '@reactor-team/js-sdk'\n\nconst reactor = new Reactor({ modelName: 'reactor/lingbot' })\nconst picker = document.querySelector('input[type=\"file\"]')\nif (!(picker instanceof HTMLInputElement)) {\n  throw new Error('Pick a seed image')\n}\nconst file = picker.files?.[0]\nif (file === undefined) {\n  throw new Error('Pick a seed image')\n}\nconst image = await reactor.uploadFile(file)\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_image', { image })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_prompt', {\n  prompt: 'A narrow stone alley at night, wet cobbles, one lit shop window.',\n})\nawait reactor.sendCommand('start', {})\n```\n\nHelios can take the same `File` with `set_conditioning` so prompt and image land together.\n\nOrbis takes an optional seed image. Send `set_image` before `set_prompt` and `start`. Use a 16:9 image, because Orbis resizes other shapes without a crop. A new image during a run has no effect until `reset`.\n\n## Browser session options\n\nOrbis reads these on the next `start`. Keep them in client state. Send them with `sendCommand` after `connect`. They are not token-mint fields.\n\n```ts\nimport { Reactor } from '@reactor-team/js-sdk'\n\nconst reactor = new Reactor({ modelName: 'reactor/visko-orbis-stable' })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_resolution', { resolution: '2k' })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_seed', { seed: 42 })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_audio_enabled', { audio_enabled: true })\n```\n\n| Option | Command | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `resolution` | `set_resolution` | `1080p`, `2k`, or `4k` delivery tier |\n| `seed` | `set_seed` | RNG seed for the next run |\n| `audioEnabled` | `set_audio_enabled` | When `false`, skip audio compute |\n| `audioPrompt` | `set_audio_prompt` | Sound description, or `\"\"` for picture-driven audio |\n\n## Custom endpoint\n\n```ts\nimport { reactorWorld } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor'\n\nconst apiKey = process.env.REACTOR_API_KEY ?? ''\nconst adapter = reactorWorld('visko-orbis-stable', {\n  apiKey,\n  baseUrl: 'https://api.reactor.inc',\n})\n```\n\n## What you have now\n\nA server call that mints a scoped Reactor token for one world or video model. Next: connect in the browser as shown in [World Generation](../media/world-generation) or [Live Generation](../media/live-generation).\n"}
